1
00:00:00,060 --> 00:00:02,110
A Roman soldier raised his spear on a Friday

2
00:00:02,170 --> 00:00:04,305
afternoon, and finished a sentence God had

3
00:00:04,346 --> 00:00:05,522
started writing over five hundred years earlier.

4
00:00:06,197 --> 00:00:09,096
In Zechariah twelve, the LORD himself is speaking.

5
00:00:09,663 --> 00:00:11,577
And he claims the wound as his own.

6
00:00:12,065 --> 00:00:13,817
and they shall look upon me whom they have

7
00:00:13,898 --> 00:00:16,738
pierced, and they shall mourn for him, as one

8
00:00:16,818 --> 00:00:19,062
mourneth for his only son Look upon ME.

9
00:00:19,834 --> 00:00:20,482
Mourn for HIM.

10
00:00:21,587 --> 00:00:23,661
The pierced one is the LORD himself, come in

11
00:00:23,681 --> 00:00:23,981
the flesh.

12
00:00:24,290 --> 00:00:25,642
John watched the spear go in.

13
00:00:26,453 --> 00:00:28,595
And he reached for that old sentence: They

14
00:00:28,635 --> 00:00:30,389
shall look on him whom they pierced.

15
00:00:30,537 --> 00:00:31,789
The soldier saw a dying man.

16
00:00:32,618 --> 00:00:34,553
John saw God keeping his own word.

17
00:00:36,051 --> 00:00:37,304
And hear how the promise begins.

18
00:00:38,076 --> 00:00:38,785
I will pour.

19
00:00:39,599 --> 00:00:40,107
Not wrath.

20
00:00:40,857 --> 00:00:42,935
The spirit of grace and of supplications.

21
00:00:43,842 --> 00:00:45,355
He gives the tears he asks for.

22
00:00:46,106 --> 00:00:47,259
God did not send a stranger.

23
00:00:47,771 --> 00:00:48,662
He came himself.

24
00:00:48,871 --> 00:00:49,902
So do what the verse says.

25
00:00:50,956 --> 00:00:51,362
Look at him.

26
00:00:52,334 --> 00:00:54,507
Let the grace he pours turn looking into mourning,

27
00:00:54,970 --> 00:00:56,353
and mourning into trust.

28
00:00:57,524 --> 00:00:58,960
Look, and live.
